<message conversation_id="10">
  <ts>2020-04-01T04:30:13.411000</ts>
  <user>Kriti</user>
  <text>@hot9cups I mean: do it like this ```pydef show(arg = None): if arg is None: arg = [] print(arg) return arg```</text>
</message>
<message conversation_id="10">
  <ts>2020-04-01T04:30:34.292000</ts>
  <user>Kriti</user>
  <text>that's different because each time the function runs it gets a fresh list</text>
</message>
<message conversation_id="10">
  <ts>2020-04-01T04:30:39.506000</ts>
  <user>Kriti</user>
  <text>wheras the other way it's always the same list</text>
</message>
<message conversation_id="10">
  <ts>2020-04-01T04:30:39.622000</ts>
  <user>Neisha</user>
  <text>basically you run off a list of the keys once use that to match and any successful matches can just be used to pull values from the dict</text>
</message>
<message conversation_id="10">
  <ts>2020-04-01T04:30:44.469000</ts>
  <user>Kriti</user>
  <text>a subtle annoyance</text>
</message>
