  <user>Dietrich</user>
  <text>Hey guys this might not have too much to do with python but i am writing a research paper for my class and I need to explain the goal of pattern recognition. I dont really know how to explain this. Can someone help me?</text>
</message>
<message conversation_id="32">
  <ts>2020-04-01T16:34:10.622000</ts>
  <user>Ioseb</user>
  <text>I like that this is in the official Python functional programming HOWTO at &lt;https://docs.python.org/3/howto/functional.html&gt;:&gt; Fredrik Lundh once suggested the following set of rules for refactoring uses of lambda:&gt; &gt; 1. Write a lambda function.&gt; 2. Write a comment explaining what the heck that lambda does.&gt; 3. Study the comment for a while and think of a name that captures the essence of the comment.&gt; 4. Convert the lambda to a def statement using that name.&gt; 5. Remove the comment.</text>
</message>
