  <ts>2020-04-02T07:04:19.758000</ts>
  <user>Vadhir</user>
  <text>@miyamoto There are some cases when generators are better to useFor example this case:```pydef get_numbers(): output = [] for i in range(100): output.append(make_number_weird(i)) return output# using generatorsdef get_numbers(): for i in range(100):  yield make_number_weird(i)```</text>
</message>
<message conversation_id="68">
  <ts>2020-04-02T07:04:41.687000</ts>
  <user>Vadhir</user>
  <text>This case will return a generator but you can easily convert it into a list</text>
</message>
<message conversation_id="68">
  <ts>2020-04-02T07:05:56.039000</ts>
  <user>Esteve</user>
  <text>@F4zi</text>
</message>
<message conversation_id="68">
  <ts>2020-04-02T07:06:29.216000</ts>
  <user>Esteve</user>
  <text>So Instead of storing all the values in a list and using them thereafter with the generator I only use the values one by one</text>
</message>
