</message>
<message conversation_id="121">
  <ts>2020-04-03T09:16:49.626000</ts>
  <user>Bryceon</user>
  <text>if I use defaultdict can I just do:```pythondict = defaultdict(int)list = ['apple apple blueberry onion']for i in list: dict[i] += 1 ```</text>
</message>
<message conversation_id="121">
  <ts>2020-04-03T09:17:07.658000</ts>
  <user>Anabelle</user>
  <text>```pyfrom collections import Counter defaultdictfruits = ['apple orange banana grapefruit orange apple apple orange banana']print(Counter(fruits))my_dict = defaultdict(int)for fruit in fruits: my_dict[fruit] += 1print(my_dict)```</text>
</message>
<message conversation_id="121">
  <ts>2020-04-03T09:17:09.841000</ts>
  <user>Anabelle</user>
  <text>yep</text>
</message>
<message conversation_id="121">
  <ts>2020-04-03T09:17:19.697000</ts>
  <user>Bryceon</user>
  <text>ahh okay</text>
</message>
<message conversation_id="121">
  <ts>2020-04-03T09:17:19.878000</ts>
  <user>Anabelle</user>
  <text>```pyCounter({'apple': 3 orange': 3 banana': 2 grapefruit': 1})defaultdict(&lt;class int'&gt; {'apple': 3 orange': 3 banana': 2 grapefruit': 1})```</text>
</message>
<message conversation_id="121">
