<message conversation_id="162">
  <ts>2020-04-04T05:42:56.730000</ts>
  <user>Sali</user>
  <text>&gt; Cython does some neat optimizations that can make things just a tad bit fasterCythonizing something like this makes pretty minimal optimizations since it's still calling to the Python C API```pythondef py_loop(): x = 0 for i in range(50): x += i```</text>
</message>
<message conversation_id="162">
  <ts>2020-04-04T05:43:46.614000</ts>
  <user>Sali</user>
  <text>But then if you optimize it suddenly you're actually using a C loop```pythondef cy_loop(): cdef int x = 0 cdef int i for i in range(50): x += i```</text>
</message>
